+# Compatibility research consulted
+
+Consulted 2026-08-14 using live network access.
+
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base, “VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1: Transition from standalone SRM and VR 9.0.2” — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/ — Applied the minimal-footprint sequence: delete the active replication, unregister and remove both standalone products before vCenter 9.1, then deploy the unified 9.1 appliance and recreate pairing and replication.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base, “Steps to Converge to VMware Live Recovery Appliance 9.0.4 (or newer) and Common Issues During Convergence” — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/408127/ — Confirmed that an in-place move from separate appliances to the unified form is unsupported and that both sites must be prepared before pairing is restored.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base, “Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to back-in-time restriction” — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/ — Confirmed the 9.1 target builds and the forward-only build-date constraint; the inventoried 4.2.3.3/8.0 U3 sources do not cross the cited newer-build boundary.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base, “Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products” — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/ — Applied the core management-plane sequence of NSX, vCenter, then ESXi, with NSX finalization at or after the host stage.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base, “VMware Cloud Foundation 9 ESXi Host and NSX VIB Upgrade Consolidation” — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436389/ — Confirmed that NSX host VIBs move with the ESXi image in VCF 9 rather than through a separate host-maintenance stage.
+- Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix, interoperability and upgrade-path views — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/ — Cross-checked the inventoried vCenter 8.0 U3, ESXi/vSAN 8.0 U3, NSX 4.2.3.3, Live Site Recovery 9.0.2, and vSphere Replication 9.0.2 source families. The reproducible design uses the compatible pinned targets vCenter 9.1.0.0.25370922, ESXi/vSAN 9.1.0.0.25370933, NSX 9.1.0.0.25318225, and unified VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1.0.0.25367487.
